A||||6||roadwarrior||What to look for on a 86gt||||14||
Z||000000||roadwarrior||11-13-2001||11:41 PM||||I'm going to go look at an 86 gt tomorow night and was just wondering if there was anything specific I should look for that might be a problem area, I already know to very closely at the frame & cradle, any info would be very helpful, thanks in advance.<P>Mitch||||reg||14
Z||000001||Jncomutt||11-14-2001||12:47 AM||||I would say the usual.<P>Listen for engine knock.  Make sure no milky oil.  Check the anti-freeze.. electrical issues, headlights, clutch movement..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Adrift||11-14-2001||01:03 AM||||pull up the carpet in the trunk to check for rust.. also, because its an ontario car, pull up the carpets - you'll notice that the vents on the floorboard have rusted through (just pull up the electrical taped areas and you'll see right through the bottom of your car! Most owners don't know these holes exist, you can use them to bargain the price of the car down (It will cost me at least $1000 to get those holes welded up!)<BR>Good luck<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||roadwarrior||11-14-2001||10:27 AM||||aight thanks for the info guys, I was just looking for anything specific to the gt's, I know about the holes and I've got the equipement to do all that kind of stuff so it's a really good deal or a really bad car at 700$ cause he doesn't want to store it for the winter.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||11-14-2001||05:11 PM||||Canadian cars are probably more prone to rust.  The real issue is that these cars just beg to be driven hard and as they are all fairly old, you want the mechanics to be sound.  Make sure all the electrics work properly as well.<P>No storage space is probably the oldest line in the used car world.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mark||11-14-2001||07:31 PM||||If it looks like this, you should buy it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86gt01.jpg_1.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Kasdan||11-14-2001||08:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mark:<BR><B>If it looks like this, you should buy it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86gt01.jpg_1.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hah, mine looked like that when i bought it....turns out the wireing had been ripped apart by everyone and his brother and the motor threw a rod a few months later and had a bad radiator.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
